<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Speakers | TEDxGIIS Youth</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" type="image/png">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.tedxgiis.app/speakers">
    <style>
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..40,100..1000;1,9..40,100..1000&family=Inter:ital,opsz,wght@0,14..32,100..900;1,14..32,100..900&display=swap');
        :root {
            --bg: #000000;
            --panel: #111111;
            --panel-strong: #1a1a1a;
            --panel-alt: #151515;
            --red: #EB0028;
            --red-dark: #b8001f;
            --text: #ffffff;
            --muted: #d7d7d7;
            --soft: #8e8e8e;
            --line: rgba(255,255,255,.08);
        }
        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
        body, html {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
            overflow-x: hidden;
        }
        h1, h2, h3 {
            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
        }
        p {
            color: var(--muted);
            line-height: 1.6;
            margin: 0;
        }
        .nav {
            background: rgba(0,0,0,.85);
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
            -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
            width: 100%;
            min-height: 3.8em;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            padding: .5em 1em;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            position: fixed;
            top: 0;
            z-index: 100;
        }
        #logopng { height: 2.6em; }
        .nav-right {
            margin-left: auto;
            display: flex;
            gap: .5rem;
            align-items: center;
            width: max-content;
            max-width: 100%;
        }
        .nav-menu { margin-left: auto; position: relative; display: none; }
        .nav-toggle { display: none; cursor: pointer; list-style: none; color: #fff; padding: .6rem .8rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; font-size: .92em; }
        .nav-toggle::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
        @media (min-width: 769px) { .nav-menu > .nav-right { display: flex !important; } }
        .menu-icon, .menu-icon::before, .menu-icon::after { display: block; width: 1.2rem; height: 2px; background: currentColor; border-radius: 2px; }
        .menu-icon { position: relative; }
        .menu-icon::before, .menu-icon::after { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; }
        .menu-icon::before { top: -6px; }
        .menu-icon::after { top: 6px; }
        .ciclk {
            color: #fff;
            text-decoration: none;
            padding: .7rem .95rem;
            position: relative;
            white-space: nowrap;
            font-weight: 600;
        }
        .ciclk::before {
            content: '';
            position: absolute;
            left: 0;
            right: 0;
            bottom: 0;
            height: 4px;
            background: transparent;
            transform: scaleX(0);
            transform-origin: left;
            transition: transform .18s ease, background-color .18s ease;
        }
        .ciclk:hover::before, .ciclk.active::before { background: #EB0028; transform: scaleX(1); }
        .page {
            max-width: 1040px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 6.2em 1.1em 2.5em;
        }
        .hero {
            border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
            border-radius: 18px;
            background: linear-gradient(145deg, #151515, #090909);
            padding: 2em;
            box-shadow: 0 18px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
        }
        .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.1em, 5vw, 3.4em); }
        .speaker-section { margin-top: 2em; }
        .speaker-section h2 {
            margin-bottom: .9em;
            font-size: clamp(1.25em, 2vw, 1.6em);
            color: #EB0028;
        }
        .cards {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
            gap: 1em;
        }
        .speaker-card {
            background: linear-gradient(145deg, #1a1a1a, #0a0a0a);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);
            border-radius: 14px;
            padding: 1em;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
            transition: transform .2s ease, border-color .2s ease;
        }
        .speaker-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-2px);
            border-color: rgba(235, 0, 40, 0.5);
        }
        .image-placeholder {
            height: 170px;
            border: 2px dashed #4a4a4a;
            border-radius: 10px;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            color: #9a9a9a;
            font-size: .95em;
            margin-bottom: .85em;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 0.75rem;
        }
        .speaker-image {
            display: block;
            width: 100%;
            height: 170px;
            object-fit: cover;
            object-position: center;
            border-radius: 10px;
            margin-bottom: .85em;
            background: #222;
        }
        .speaker-name {
            color: #EB0028;
            font-size: 1.1em;
            font-weight: 700;
        }
        .speaker-meta {
            font-size: .94em;
            color: #cecece;
            margin-top: .35em;
            line-height: 1.55;
        }
        footer {
            border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
            margin-top: 2.5em;
            padding-top: 1.2em;
            color: #8e8e8e;
            font-size: .9em;
        }
        @media (max-width: 900px) { .cards { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .nav { padding: .5em; }
            #logopng { height: 2.2em; }
            .desktop-nav { display: none; }
            .nav-menu { display: block; }
            .nav-toggle { display: block; }
            .nav-menu .nav-right { display: flex; position: absolute; top: calc(100% + .5rem); right: 0; width: max-content; max-width: 100dvw; padding: .45rem; flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; gap: .15rem; background: rgba(0,0,0,.96); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(0,0,0,.35); }
            .nav-menu:not([open]) .nav-right { display: none; }
            .nav-menu .ciclk { padding: .75rem .8rem; font-size: .92em; white-space: normal; }
            .hero { padding: 1.4em; }
            .page { padding-left: .8rem; padding-right: .8rem; }
        }
        @media (max-width: 560px) { .cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="nav">
        <img src="/resources/logo-white.png" alt="TEDxGIIS Logo" id="logopng">
        <nav class="nav-right desktop-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
            <a href="/" class="ciclk">Home</a>
            <a href="/speakers" class="ciclk active">Speakers</a>
            <a href="/team" class="ciclk">Team</a>
           
        </nav>
        <details class="nav-menu">
            <summary class="nav-toggle" aria-label="Open navigation"><span class="menu-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <div class="nav-right">
                <a href="/" class="ciclk">Home</a>
                <a href="/speakers" class="ciclk active">Speakers</a>
                <a href="/team" class="ciclk">Team</a>
                
            </div>
        </details>
    </div>

    <main class="page">
        <section class="hero">
            <h1>Speaker List</h1>
            <p>Meet the voices shaping TEDxGIIS Youth.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="speaker-section">
            <div class="cards">
                <article class="speaker-card">
                  <img src="/resources/Suchandra Roychowdhury .jpeg" alt="Suchandra Roychowdhury" class="speaker-image">
                  <p class="speaker-name">Suchandra Roychowdhury</p>
                  <p class="speaker-meta">Author, educator, and travel enthusiast Suchandra Roychowdhury lives in Bayshore, Singapore. She studied English Literature and obtained her Master of Arts from Presidency College before pursuing an MPhil at the University of Calcutta. Her debut novel, &quot;The Shotgun Wedding,&quot; was a bestseller for Aleph Book Company and was shortlisted for the Women AutHer Awards 2023 by the Times of India Group. It has since been translated into French, Spanish, and German and displayed at the 2024 Frankfurt Book Fair. She has also written a collection of Bengali plays, &quot;Armani o Jamdani.&quot; Her next novel, &quot;Who Lit the First Flame,&quot; is scheduled for release in November 2026.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="speaker-card">
                    <img src="/resources/Mantazh Khanna.jpeg" alt="Mantazh Khanna" class="speaker-image">
                    <p class="speaker-name">Mantazh Khanna</p>
                     <p class="speaker-meta">Mantazh Khanna is a neuroscience and mindfulness expert, speaker, researcher, and host of the podcast THINK SHIFT with Mantazh. A Harvard Business School MBA and former corporate leader, she spent nearly two decades leading brands and businesses before turning her focus to understanding the human brain. She is currently pursuing a PhD in Natural Medicine, researching how neuroscience and contemplative practices can strengthen cognitive health and human potential. A cancer survivor and lifelong student of the mind, Mantazh brings together science, lived experience, and practical tools to help people better understand and train their brains for greater resilience, self-awareness, and wellbeing.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="speaker-card">
                    <img src="/resources/Mahasweta Paul.jpeg" alt="Dr. Mahasweta Paul" class="speaker-image">
                    <p class="speaker-name">Dr. Mahasweta Paul</p>
                     <p class="speaker-meta">Mahasweta Paul, PhD, is a biochemical engineer and Research Fellow at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, specializing in drug-delivery systems, sustainable food, and reactor technologies. She holds a PhD in Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering from NTU and an MTech in Biotechnology from Jadavpur University, India. Beyond the bench, Dr. Paul is a committed science advocate and founder and advisor to the Society of Women Engineers at NTU. She currently drives community engagement with POWERS to support women in STEM initiatives and has also served as a Lead Curator and Advisor for TEDxNTU. At the intersection of science, people, and possibility, she is interested in how researchers can translate complex ideas into solutions and stories that create meaningful impact.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="speaker-card">
                    <img src="/resources/Anju Sharma.jpeg" alt="Dr. Anju Sharma" class="speaker-image">
                    <p class="speaker-name">Dr. Anju Sharma</p>
                     <p class="speaker-meta">Dr. Anju Sharma is an educator and Hindi scholar with experience across higher education and international schooling. She holds an MPhil and PhD in Hindi and has taught at the University of Delhi. She later transitioned into school education, contributing to the early development of IB Hindi and serving as a global IB examiner. Her career has brought her into collaboration with educators across diverse cultural and academic contexts. Her work reflects a deep commitment to language, learning, values, and the role of education in shaping confidence, perspective, and character.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="speaker-card">
                    <img src="/resources/Uday.jpeg" alt="Uday Singh Yadava" class="speaker-image">
                    <p class="speaker-name">Uday Singh Yadava</p>
                     <p class="speaker-meta">Uday Singh Yadava is fascinated by the questions that sit beneath everyday life: what gives us purpose, what makes an idea matter, and how we decide what is worth caring about. A young advocate and storyteller, his interests span youth engagement, education, sustainability, and the ways curiosity can become meaningful action. Through youth-led initiatives and educational communities, he enjoys bringing different perspectives together and making complex ideas feel personal and relevant. He is particularly interested in questions of purpose and identity. Away from his work, Uday is an avid reader of classic literature, with a particular fondness for War and Peace, which he has read cover to cover twice.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <footer>© 2026 TEDxGIIS Youth. This independent TEDx event is operated under licence from TED.</footer>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
